{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  PMost Latin American currencies edged higher on Monday, as the U.S. dollar pulled back, while equities were a mixed bag as investors weighed the latest flare-up in the Middle East.MSCI's Latin American currency index (.MILA00000CUS) gained 0.2% and was on track to clock in a second cons…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American currencies edged higher on Monday, as the U.S. dollar pulled back, while equities were a mixed bag as investors weighed the latest flare-up in ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/","linkText":"the Middle East"}},"."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Latin American currency index (.MILA00000CUS) gained 0.2% and was on track to clock in a second consecutive monthly advance helped by a broadly softer dollar through August."]},{"type":"p","children":["The greenback, however, has recovered recently as expectations of a September rate hike by the U.S. Federal Reserve increased after Fed Chair Kevin Warsh said policymakers will \"have work to do\" if inflation didn't fall to the bank's 2% target."]},{"type":"p","children":["The dollar index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}},", which measures the U.S. currency against six major peers, dipped 0.2% on Monday, supporting regional currencies."]},{"type":"p","children":["Crude prices rose more than 2% after ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/us/","linkText":"the U.S."}}," attacked an Iranian island in the Strait of Hormuz and Tehran said it had retaliated."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Latin American stock index (.MILA00000PUS) added 0.4%, but was still headed for monthly losses."]},{"type":"p","children":["In ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/brazil/","linkText":"Brazil"}},", equities ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," jumped 0.9% and were on track to clock in their ninth straight day of gains, with oil giant Petrobras ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3","text":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3"}}," the biggest boost on the benchmark index, up 2.5%."]},{"type":"p","children":["However, Brazil's economy likely grew at a slower pace in the previous quarter, a Reuters poll showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Central bank data showed the nation's gross debt as a share of gross domestic product rose to 82.5% in July from 81.9% a month earlier."]},{"type":"p","children":["Against this backdrop, Brazilian Vice President Geraldo Alckmin said the country has room both to restrain public spending and accelerate economic growth, arguing that such a combination would help reduce the debt-to-GDP ratio."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The significant rise in public debt continues to stand out,\" XP economist Tiago Sbardelotto said, noting that gross debt reached its highest level since April 2021 while net debt hit a record high."]},{"type":"p","children":["Finance Minister Dario Durigan said that some social programs could eventually cease to be mandatory expenditures, a move he said would give policymakers greater flexibility in managing the federal budget."]},{"type":"p","children":["The real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," jumped 0.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colombia's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCOP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCOP"}}," extended its drop after getting pummeled in Friday's session after the country's budget bill revealed a far deeper deficit than markets had expected for 2026 and 2027."]},{"type":"p","children":["The currency was set for its worst month since July 2025 after a strong run so far this year. Stocks in Bogota ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BVC:ICAP","text":"BVC:ICAP"}}," advanced 0.7%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Chilean peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol"